          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: le réveillon",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "le réveillon — \"the festive late-night dinner (24 or 31 December)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Toute la famille passe le réveillon chez ma tante. The whole family spends the festive dinner at my aunt's."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It falls on the evenings of 24 and 31 December."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "réveillon is built on réveiller \"to wake up\", from veiller \"to stay awake\", which is inherited from Latin vigilāre \"to keep watch\" (Lewis & Short)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
